  "term": "method of right and wrong cases",
  "definition": "In historical psychophysics, the method of right and wrong cases is an error method in which two stimuli that differ only slightly are presented and the observer judges which seems greater. It was used to study how accurately small differences in sensation or perception can be detected.",
